# Dodging: an attack that lands hurts, the same attack met with a dodge does not.
#
# The boss's windup is forced with `set` so the timing is the same in every game; left to
# its brain, the boss would pick its attacks at random. The dodge is played by a
# player-scope agent, through the same controls a human has.
#
# Written for the CURRENT sandbox (e5 player, e6 boss, e7 and e8 skeletons).

seed 42

# --- the arena as the game spawns it, whatever was played in it before
act heal id=e5
act heal id=e6
act set id=e5 component=Health value='{"current":100,"max":100}'
act set id=e5 component=Stamina path=current value=80
act set id=e5 component=Action value=Idle
act stop
act teleport id=e5 x=0 z=-2
act teleport id=e6 x=0 z=-6
act teleport id=e7 x=-19 z=-19
act teleport id=e8 x=19 z=-19
invariant field e5 Health.current > 0

# --- 1. not dodged: an IceSlam 4 m away lands for 30
act set id=e6 component=Action value='{"Windup":{"attack":"IceSlam","left":0.1}}'
expect shows e6 "windup IceSlam"
expect field e5 Health.current == 100
step 20
expect journal "e6 -> e5 IceSlam -30"
expect field e5 Health.current == 70

# --- 2. dodged: the same windup, and the player rolls sideways as a player-scope agent
mark
act set id=e5 component=Action value=Idle
act teleport id=e5 x=0 z=-2
act set id=e6 component=Action value='{"Windup":{"attack":"IceSlam","left":0.1}}'
session --agent bot --scope player
act? teleport id=e5 x=0 z=0
expect result contains "needs dev scope"
act dodge dir=E
expect result contains "ok: dodging E"
session --agent scenario      # time is the dev agent's to control
step 20
expect journal "e5 dodged IceSlam from e6"
expect !journal "e6 -> e5"
expect field e5 Health.current == 70
expect field e5 Stamina.current < 80
